## v0.4+ - Referential Memory (the BBS)
Decisions mostly locked; see docs/bbs-design.md. Post-0.3.0 at the earliest.
[ ] Persistent threaded store: "files, but threaded, persistent, cross-session"
[ ] Commands under @variant namespace: /bbs@list /bbs@search /bbs@read
    /bbs@post /bbs@reply /bbs@archive /bbs@pin /bbs@delete
[ ] LOCKED principle: AI never reads/writes BBS itself - USER tool only.
    @search returns titles/ids only; @read is the explicit pull (like /file);
    every model-bound byte stays explicit.
[ ] @read mirrors /file's three forms (bare / chat-coupled / :ai pipeline)
[ ] Clean-room reimplement from the existing core: keep filesystem/stdlib/
    cat-debuggable threads+index+summaries+artifacts; drop roles & swarm caps
    for v1; defer fork/collapse and :bbs pipeline sinks
[ ] Cross-platform locking (existing core is fcntl/unix-only)
[ ] Default root ~/.pyttai/bbs/, container-mountable like /sessions
